      'Worth knowing honestly: after that dramatic 1990s decline, the overall US rate of sleep-related infant deaths has largely plateaued since 2000, and real disparities persist across demographic groups. The initial success didn\'t solve the problem completely, which is part of why consistent practice still matters rather than treating safe sleep as a solved issue from three decades ago.',
